## 🤖 Cursor AI 프롬프트: SK쉴더스 리뉴얼 코딩 컨벤션 설정

[System Instruction]
You are my AI pair programmer for the "SK Shields Renewal" project. From this point forward, you must strictly adhere to the following coding conventions for all code you generate, edit, or refactor.

1. Naming Convention: camelCase
   All folders, files (except for components), variables, and function names must use camelCase.

- Variables & Functions:

Good: const userProfile = {};, function getUserData() {}

Bad: const user_profile = {};, const UserProfile = {};

- Folders & Non-Component Files:

Good: /utils/formatDate.ts

Bad: /utils/FormatDate.ts

❗️ Exception: React Components
React component filenames and the component functions/classes themselves must use PascalCase.

Good: Filename ImageUploader.tsx, Component export default function ImageUploader() {}

2. CSS Styling Methodology: BEM
   All SCSS class names written in .module.scss files must follow the BEM (Block\_\_Element--Modifier) methodology. The goal is to create readable, reusable, and conflict-free styles.

- BEM Structure:

Block: The standalone component root. (e.g., .card)

Element: A part of the block. Use a double underscore. (e.g., .card\_\_title)

Modifier: A variation or state of a block or element. Use a double hyphen. (e.g., .card--dark, .card\_\_button--disabled)

- Example Implementation:
  You must follow this pattern when creating components and styles.

JSX Structure:

JavaScript

<div className={styles.card}>
  <h2 className={styles.card__title}>Card Title</h2>
  <button className={`${styles.card__button} ${styles['card__button--primary']}`}>
    Action
  </button>
</div>
Corresponding module.scss (with nesting):

SCSS

.card {
/_ Block styles _/
border: 1px solid #eee;

&\_\_title {
/_ Element styles _/
font-size: 1.2rem;
}

&\_\_button {
/_ Element styles _/
padding: 8px;

    &--primary {
      /* Modifier styles */
      background-color: blue;
      color: white;
    }

}
}
Please confirm you understand and will apply these rules to all future code.
